# Power Chords: Palm-Muted Gallop (repertoire plan: st-power-chords-gallop). An original riff in
# E minor. The gallop is an eighth and two sixteenths on the open string 6 (E), palm muted, picked
# strictly down, down, up. Between the gallops come accented, unmuted power chords, all downstrokes:
# A5 (577xxx), G5 (355xxx), C5 (x355xx), D5 (x577xx), fingers 1, 3 and 4 in every shape.
# Bars 1-2 call (gallops, then A5, then G5 to A5); bars 3-4 answer on string 5 (C5, then C5 to D5);
# bars 5-6 call again; bar 7 is the answer's last bar, and the riff lands on a ringing open E5
# (022xxx), the i chord. Every jump to a chord comes after open-string gallops, so the fretting hand
# has a whole beat or more to get there.
title: Power Chords: Palm-Muted Gallop
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original riff
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 5
tags: power chords, palm muting, gallop, rock, metal, riff
tempo: 100
time: 4/4
key: Em

